WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:17.240
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.750
to air in 2022.
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.590
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:30.079
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:00:30.079 --> 00:00:34.690
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:39.980
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:45.140
That's Fire And Blood volume 1. The yet unreleased
Fire And Blood volume 2 will continue from

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:50.809
where part 1 ended, with Rhaenyra Targaryen's
son Aegon lll's reign and will cover Blackyre

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:56.170
rebellions, war with Dorne and go all the
way to the Mad King and Robert's Rebellion

00:00:56.170 --> 00:01:00.280
that ended Targaryen dynasty.
The key event of the prequel will be the Dance

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:05.040
of the Dragon, a Targaryen civil war.
This summer, it was reported and recently

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:10.250
confirmed by Entertainment Weekly that HBO
has released a casting call for Princess Rhaenyra

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:15.060
Targaryen, a key figure from this time period
of the Dance of the Dragons.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:18.500
The casting call describes her: “King Viserys’
chosen heir,

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:23.020
a dragon rider who grew up expecting to become
the first ruling Queen of Westeros.”

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:28.720
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve
as showrunners and executive producers. George

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:31.870
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive
producer.

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:35.930
The Dance of the Dragons was the most devastating
war in the history of the Seven Kingdoms.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:41.340
A war of succession between Aegon II and his
half-sister Rhaenyra over their father Viserys

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.320
I's throne.
Both of them thought they belonged on the

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:48.700
Iron Throne. When people started declaring
for one of them or the other, their fight

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:54.401
divided the kingdoms in two. Targaryens fought
Targaryens, bothers fought brothers, dragons

00:01:54.401 --> 00:01:59.320
fought dragons. By the time it was over, thousands
were dead. The conflict would prove to be

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.920
incredibly destructive for not only House
Targaryen, but large parts of Westeros as

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:09.340
well. In addition, it devastated the Targaryen's
dragon population, ultimately leading to their

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:12.890
extinction within a few decades.
They never truly recovered.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:17.811
By the end of the reign of King Viserys I
Targaryen, twenty dragons were alive. The

00:02:17.811 --> 00:02:23.450
majority of these died during the civil war
called the Dance of the Dragons, which began

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:29.260
in 129 AC and lasted until mid 131 AC.
One of the main characters in this series

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:33.881
is going to be Rhaenyra Targaryen.
Princess Rhaenyra Targaryen, cheered as the

00:02:33.881 --> 00:02:38.460
Realm's Delight when she was young
and later called the Half-Year Queen, was

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:44.470
the first-born child of King Viserys I Targaryen.
Rhaenyra was King Viserys I's only living

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:48.130
child by his first wife,Queen Aemma of House
Arryn.

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:51.370
At the age of eight she was made her father's
hei

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:56.020
and grew up expecting to become the first
ruling Queen of Westeros.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:59.130
Rhaenyra was a dragonrider whose mount was
Syrax.

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:04.600
Rhaenyra had her family's Valyrian looks,
wearing her silver-gold hair in a long braid

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:10.070
in the manner of Queen Visenya Targaryen.
Beautiful as a child, Rhaenyra was later declared

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:14.520
by her uncle, Prince Daemon Targaryen,
to be the most beautiful maiden in all the

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.599
Seven Kingdoms.
Due to the lack of a male heir, Viserys designated

00:03:18.599 --> 00:03:23.270
Rhaenyra as his successor.
Therefore, Rhaenyra was the only female Targaryen

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:28.820
to lay claim to the Iron Throne in her own
right. Since she was raised as designated

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:34.459
heir, Rhaenyra became quite pampered and arrogant,
but also gained practical governmental experience.

00:03:34.459 --> 00:03:40.510
After Rhaenyra's mother died, her father remarried
and had several sons with his second wife,

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:45.420
Alicent of House Hightower.
Even so, Viserys still publicly expected his

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:49.900
daughter to succeed him,
and when he died, his official will even stated

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.200
so.
However, Rhaenyra's younger half-brother,

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:56.880
Aegon, challenged her claim.
He stated that the normal inheritance laws

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:03.360
of the Andals (which formed the basis of the
unified law code in Westeros) called for male-preference

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:08.680
primogeniture, meaning that a younger son
would rightfully inherit before an older daughter.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:14.220
Rhaenyra had 2 husbands and 5 sons. Her first
husband was Laenor of House Velayrion,

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:19.340
son of the Sea Snake. Laenor and Rhaenyra
had three sons together: Princes Jacaerys

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.830
'Jace',
Lucerys 'Luke', and Joffrey 'Joff' Velaryon.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:27.910
All were near adulthood and had dragons of
their own when Rhaenyra's father, Viserys

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:31.570
I, died.
It was rumored that those sons of Rhaenyra's

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.260
were actually fathered by her champion and
lover,

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:38.570
Harwin Strong, the strongest man in Westeros,
called "Breakbones",

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:43.430
as all three were born with brown hair and
brown eyes, though Laenor and Rhaenyra both

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:48.340
had light silver/gold hair and purple eyes.
The Greens were the ones who sparked this

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:53.870
rumor, often calling them Strongs. The true
parentage of Rhaenyra's three eldest children

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:57.931
is still unclear.
The siblings Laenor and Laena Velaryon who

00:04:57.931 --> 00:05:04.350
were married to Rhaenyra and Daemon Targaryen,
both died in 120 AC, as did Rhaenyra's alleged

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:09.520
lover, Breakbones. Rhaenyra then secretly
married her uncle, Prince Daemon, the most

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:14.050
experienced and the most dangerous warrior
of his time, at Dragonstone. The news of their

00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:17.740
wedding caused a great scandal at the court
of King's Landing

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:23.190
and made Rhaenyra's father furious. It took
some time before Viserys and Daemon reconciled.

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:26.770
Rhaenyra's other sons, Princes Aegon and Viserys
Targaryen,

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:30.330
were fathered by Daemon and all had Targaryen
features.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:35.460
At the time of her father's death, Rhaenyra
was on Dragonstone awaiting the birth of her

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:38.600
child.
The greens in King's Landing ensured that

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:42.889
the news of the Viserys's death did not reach
her until her own supporters in the Red Keep

00:05:42.889 --> 00:05:48.380
were dead or imprisoned
and Aegon II's coronation had already occurred.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:53.180
This began a devastating civil war that tore
apart the Seven Kingdoms, known as The Dance

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:57.710
of the Dragons, as it was the only war in
which both sides had dragonriders.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:02.440
The war lasted for three years, and by the
time it came to an end nearly all of the Targaryen

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:07.450
dragons had been killed. The conflict also
resulted in the death of three of Rhaenyra's

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:11.280
five sons,
as well as the eldest son of Aegon II.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:17.160
Rhaenyra's personal sigil was the normal Targaryen
heraldry (a three-headed red dragon on a black

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:22.030
field), quartered with the moon-and-falcon
sigil of House Arryn (for her mother Aemma

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:25.419
Arryn),
and the silver seahorse on sea green of House

00:06:25.419 --> 00:06:31.411
Velaryon (for her first husband Laenor Velaryon,
as well as for the Velaryons in general, who

00:06:31.411 --> 00:06:36.670
were among her major supporters).
During the Dance, her faction used her personal

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:41.840
heraldry as their battle-flag.
Aegon II held many advantages in the war,

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:46.380
including control of the capital city,
the support of the Lord Commander of the Kingsguard,

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:51.210
and the approval of the High Septon.
Rhaenyra's faction was based at Dragonstone,

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:55.990
and to her advantage she had a larger number
of dragons under her control - twelve to Aegon's

00:06:55.990 --> 00:07:02.919
four - though three of these were "wild" dragons
and as-yet untamed, while another three were

00:07:02.919 --> 00:07:05.520
immature.
She also did not have enough Targaryen blood

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.970
relatives on her side to ride all of them,
and a dragon will (typically) the only bond

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:15.590
with someone possessing the blood of Old Valyria.
Thus a search was launched to find any surviving

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:21.370
Targaryen bastards - nicknamed the "dragonseeds"
- and enlist them in Rhaenyra's cause.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:26.979
The two factions during the war - one supporting
Aegon and the other supporting Rhaenyra –

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:31.320
became known as the "Blacks" and the "Greens"
because of the incident that took place at

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:36.680
a tournament some years before the war began.
Aegon II's mother Queen Alicent had worn a

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:41.020
green dress to the tournament
while Rhaenyra wore a black dress.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:45.860
The note was taken, and thereafter it became
the custom to refer to “greens” and “blacks”

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:50.130
when talking of the queen's party and the
party of the princess, respectively.

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:55.199
Generally, Rhaenyra was supported by noble
families who had enjoyed royal favor during

00:07:55.199 --> 00:08:01.370
her father's reign and possessed strong ties
to the crown, while Aegon II rallied those

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:07.430
who had been out of favor. Viserys I had signed
charters with many powerful Houses

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:10.169
in which they swore to accept Rhaenyra as
his heir,

00:08:10.169 --> 00:08:13.750
but at least some of them broke their word
after Viserys died.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:18.979
Rhaenyra sent her eldest son Jacaerys north
on his dragon to visit the Eyrie and then

00:08:18.979 --> 00:08:21.490
Winterfell.
At that time, the Vale was ruled by a female

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:27.460
heiress who had inherited in her own right
due to a lack of male heirs, and given that

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:30.960
the entire civil war questioned a woman's
right to rule,

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:35.919
she and Rhaenrya were natural allies.
Moreover, the Arryns had enjoyed royal favor

00:08:35.919 --> 00:08:40.909
earlier in Viserys I's reign
since his first wife - Rhaenyra's own mother

00:08:40.909 --> 00:08:45.110
- was an Arryn, thus binding the two families
by blood.

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:49.480
The Starks came into the war on Rhaenyra's
side in accordance with the original agreements

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:54.660
they had made with Viserys. Rhaenyra's second
son Lucerys flew on his dragon to Storm's

00:08:54.660 --> 00:09:00.930
End to gain an alliance with House Baratheon,
but Aegon II's brother Aemond flew to Storm's

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:04.450
End
at the same time to pursue the same goal,

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:09.279
riding the older dragon Vhagar.
The results were decidedly mixed, and Storm's

00:09:09.279 --> 00:09:15.720
End subsequently supported Aegon II.
Aemond, riding Vhagar, killed Luke over Shipbreaker

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:18.430
Bay
as he attempted to leave after failing to

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:23.970
gain Lord Borros' allegiance.
The Westerlands also sided with Aegon II because

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:28.970
he had appointed Tyland Lannister as his new
Master of Coin. The Hightowers were of course

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:34.410
staunch supporters of Aegon II,
and so apparently was much of the Reach. Dorne

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:39.300
had not been incorporated into the realm yet,
and as they have often done throughout history,

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:43.850
the Iron Islands remained neutral
while the mainlanders slaughtered each other

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:47.320
although they did the Blacks a favor when
they started attacking the Westerlands.

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:53.050
At some point during the war, Rhaenyra herself
was captured by Aegon II's forces

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:58.610
and was fed to her half-brother's dragon,
while her son was forced to watch.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:02.920
Rhaenyra's three eldest sons all died fighting
during the Dance of the Dragons,

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:07.709
but her two youngest sons, the sons by her
second husband, Prince Daemon, survived the

00:10:07.709 --> 00:10:10.900
civil war.
Rhaenyra's supporters led by House Tully and

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:15.620
House Stark continued to fight on
in the name of her two surviving sons,

00:10:15.620 --> 00:10:21.149
however, and eventually triumphed: Through
uncertain circumstances, Aegon II died without

00:10:21.149 --> 00:10:26.410
male heirs, and peace was achieved when Rhaenyra's
eldest surviving son was crowned as Aegon

00:10:26.410 --> 00:10:29.200
III.
He was the son who had been forced to watch

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:33.880
his mother consumed by a dragon,
and he developed a deep hatred and fear of

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:37.240
the creatures.
So many dragons had died in the war that the

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:42.390
Targaryens couldn't maintain a stable breeding
population, and the few survivors became inbred

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:46.170
and sickly.
The last Targaryen dragons - the last dragons

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:51.649
in the known world - died during the reign
of Aegon III, earning him the sobriquet "Aegon

00:10:51.649 --> 00:10:55.610
the Dragonbane".
Aegon III married Aegon II's surviving daughter

00:10:55.610 --> 00:11:00.390
to re-unite the factions from the war,
though many cadet branches and relatives of

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:05.750
House Targaryen had been killed in the war.
Aegon III ruled well, and both of his sons

00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:09.140
(Daeron I and Baelor I) became kings after
him,

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:15.130
but each died childless. Therefore, the throne
later passed to Rhaenyra's youngest son, Viserys

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:17.670
II,
who had served as Hand of the King under his

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:22.780
nephews for many years.
Viserys II was the father of Aegon IV and

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:27.230
grandfather of Daeron II,
and Daeron II was himself the grandfather

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:34.200
of Aerion Brightfame, Aegon V "the Unlikely",
and Maester Aemon. Neither Rhaenyra or Aegon

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:38.970
II are remembered well in the history of the
Westeros and many argue that neither side

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:42.420
truly won at the end,
but it's a fact that Rhaenyra's loyalists

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:45.480
won the war and Rhaenyra's children got the
throne.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:49.959
Let me know your thoughts about everything:
the prequel, its characters, especially Rhaenyra,

00:11:49.959 --> 00:11:56.640
in the comment section down below. Thank you
so much for watching and hope to see you in

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:59.690
the next one. Peace!

